ent-NCCyberwareServiceTool = cyberware service probe
    .desc = A contact probe for mounting, functional testing and physically disconnecting exposed cyberware.
ent-NCCyberwareServiceKit = cyberware service kit
    .desc = Ten consumable service applications for exposed frames and replaceable nodes. Cannot reverse permanent damage.
nc-cyberware-surgery-calibrate = Functional test and calibration
nc-cyberware-surgery-mount = Mount or extract an implant
nc-cyberware-surgery-disconnect = Disconnect neural interface
nc-cyberware-surgery-repair = Local cyberware service
nc-cyberware-surgery-calibration-required = Hardware mounted. Perform a separate functional test with a service probe before use. You can close the site with the hardware uncalibrated.
nc-cyberware-surgery-assembly-incomplete = Functional test failed: a required physical part is missing. Complete the assembly on a bench.
nc-cyberware-surgery-output-low = Functional test failed: mechanical output is below the required range. Repair or replace the damaged node.
nc-cyberware-surgery-signal-weak = Functional test failed: neural signal is too weak. Service the interface first.
nc-cyberware-surgery-no-power = Functional test failed: no suitable supply has enough charge for the test.
nc-cyberware-surgery-power-overload = Functional test failed: the body bus cannot grant the expected full-load draw.
nc-cyberware-surgery-overheated = Functional test failed: the hardware must cool down.
nc-cyberware-surgery-emp-disabled = Functional test failed: electronics are still disabled by EMP.
nc-cyberware-surgery-no-repair-needed = No recoverable local defect. Missing parts or permanent damage require replacement; no service material was spent.
